// src/pages/brands/zline.astro
// ZLINE brand pillar (residential). Structure cloned from brands/bluestar.astro.
// Schema approach cloned from outdoor Bull/Blaze: mergeCredentials + BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL
//   (geo-neutral, 8-branch location array, no streetAddress, no aggregateRating).
// Verified models only (web-checked): ranges RA30/36/48 (Professional dual-fuel), SGR (gas),
//   Autograph RAZ-30/36/48 (+ -G/-CB/RAZ-WM color suffixes), Paramount gas SGRZ-36.
//   Range hoods (ZLINE flagship product): KB (24-48 convertible), KECOM-30/36/42/48 (400/700 CFM),
//   587/597, 8654, KE/KZ families; wall/island/under-cabinet/insert; ducted + convertible(ductless).
//   OEM parts via zlineparts.com (direct, inexpensive) = repair-economics USP.
// Value-tier positioning: cheap, widely-available parts → repair almost always beats replace.
// Em-dash budget in visible body: keep low. Voice: "our techs" / "we".

import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE } from '../../data/branches';
import { mergeCredentials } from '../../data/credentials-schema';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../lib/build-location-array';

const phone = MAIN_PHONE;
const phoneRaw = MAIN_PHONE.replace(/\D/g, '');
const phoneHref = `tel:+1${phoneRaw}`;
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/zline/";

const title = "ZLINE Range and Hood Repair Los Angeles — Same Day";
const description = `ZLINE range, dual-fuel, and range hood repair across SoCal. Professional RA, Autograph RAZ, KECOM and KB hoods. Cheap OEM parts, fast turnaround. $89 diagnostic. ${phone}.`;

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What ZLINE appliances do you repair in Los Angeles?",
    a: "The full ZLINE cooking lineup. Ranges across the Professional series (RA30, RA36, RA48 dual fuel; SGR gas) and the Autograph Edition (RAZ-30, RAZ-36, RAZ-48 with the gold, champagne-bronze, and matte-white accents, plus the Paramount SGRZ-36 gas range), rangetops, wall ovens, gas cooktops, and the product ZLINE is most known for, range hoods (the KB convertible line, the professional KECOM-30/36/42/48, the 587 and 597 wall series, 8654, and the island and under-cabinet variants). If it says ZLINE and it cooks or vents, our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair service it across all five SoCal counties."
  },
  {
    q: "ZLINE parts are cheaper than Sub-Zero or Wolf. Does that make repair worth it?",
    a: "Almost always, and this is the single most useful thing to know about owning a ZLINE. ZLINE parts are inexpensive and widely available, and ZLINE runs its own direct parts store (zlineparts.com) with no authorized-service-only gating. What that means in practice: a failed igniter, bake element, or hood blower motor is a low-cost part plus our labor and the $89 diagnostic, not the several-hundred-dollar gated part you would face on a luxury brand. Because a ZLINE range runs a few thousand dollars new (not ten-plus like Wolf), the repair-versus-replace math still favors repair for almost any single-component failure, and the fast parts pipeline means we often finish same-day."
  },
  {
    q: "My ZLINE range hood stopped pulling air. What usually fails?",
    a: "On a ZLINE hood that runs weak or not at all, our techs check three things in order. First the blower motor (the KECOM line uses a 400 or 700 CFM 4-speed motor; a motor that hums but barely spins or won't start is the most common failure). Second the speed control or switch, which can pit and drop a speed. Third the baffle filters, which when caked with grease choke airflow and make a healthy motor look weak, a cleaning rather than a part. On convertible KB hoods we also confirm whether it is running ducted or recirculating (ductless) with a spent charcoal filter, which people often forget is a consumable."
  },
  {
    q: "What's the difference between the Professional (RA) and Autograph Edition (RAZ) ranges for repair?",
    a: "Mechanically they share the same platform, so the service tree is nearly identical: gas cooktop with electric convection oven on the dual-fuel units, the same igniters, spark system, bake and broil elements, and oven sensor. The Autograph Edition (RAZ, and the SGRZ Paramount gas model) adds the gold, champagne-bronze (CB), or matte-white (WM) handle and knob accents. Those accents are cosmetic trim, not a different machine, so a repair on an RAZ-36-G runs the same diagnostic and the same core parts as an RA36. We identify the exact model from the tag before ordering so any accent-specific trim piece matches."
  },
  {
    q: "How long do ZLINE ranges and hoods last, and are they hard to get parts for?",
    a: "With normal use and repair, a ZLINE range gives 10 to 15 years and a hood often longer since a hood is mechanically simpler. Parts availability is a genuine ZLINE strength: the direct parts store carries igniters, elements, control boards, blower motors, baffle filters, and trim, so we rarely wait on a gated distributor the way we do for luxury brands. The typical wear items are predictable, oven igniter and bake element on the ranges, blower motor and filters on the hoods, and all of them are inexpensive parts."
  },
  {
    q: "My ZLINE dual-fuel oven won't heat but the burners work. What is that?",
    a: "Burners lighting while the oven stays cold points at the electric oven side, not the gas cooktop. On ZLINE dual-fuel ranges (RA and RAZ series) the usual causes are a failed bake element (visible break or blistering), a failed oven igniter on the gas-oven variants, or an oven temperature sensor reading wrong and telling the control to stop heating. Our techs isolate which on-site with a meter rather than guessing, and all three are inexpensive parts we can usually source fast from ZLINE direct. $89 diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you install new ZLINE ranges or hoods?",
    a: "No, we repair what is already installed. New range or hood installation is a gas-line and ducting trade, and custom cabinetry modification is a fabrication trade, both outside appliance repair. If your ZLINE is under its manufacturer warranty we can assess the failure and tell you whether it is warranty-eligible before any out-of-pocket work, and our own 90-day SDAR labor-and-parts warranty covers the repairs we perform. BHGS #A49573, BBB Accredited Business."
  }
];

const schemaJsons = [
