/>

<!-- 01 INTRO -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01, About this service</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">ZLINE is attainable-luxury cooking, and the parts are cheap and fast, so repair almost always wins.</h2>

    <p class="intro-speakable">ZLINE Kitchen and Bath is an American brand built around one idea: professional-style ranges and a deep range hood lineup at a price far below Wolf, Thermador, or Viking. In our six-county SoCal territory ZLINE shows up in remodeled kitchens across the full map, from Pasadena and Burbank to Irvine and Rancho Cucamonga, where owners wanted the pro-range look and the statement hood without the luxury-tier invoice. That value positioning is exactly why our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair treat ZLINE as one of the most repair-friendly brands we service.</p>

    <p>Two ZLINE realities shape every call we run. First, <strong>parts are inexpensive and widely available</strong>. ZLINE runs its own direct parts supply (zlineparts.com) that carries igniters, elements, control boards, blower motors, and baffle filters, with no authorized-service-only gate. We are not waiting on a locked luxury-brand distributor, so a common failure is often a same-day fix. Second, <strong>the range hood is ZLINE's signature product</strong>, not an afterthought. Many homes have a ZLINE hood over a different-brand range, so a large share of our ZLINE work is hood-only. This page covers both sides, the ranges and the hoods, because that is how the brand actually lands in LA kitchens.</p>

    <p>Every ZLINE service call gets a $89 residential diagnostic (applied toward the repair when work is approved), OEM ZLINE parts, and an honest written quote before any work begins. Because a ZLINE range runs a few thousand dollars rather than ten-plus, we will always tell you straight when a repair is the right call, which for a single-component failure is nearly every time.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 RANGES -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">02, ZLINE range repair</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Professional RA dual-fuel, SGR gas, Autograph RAZ and Paramount SGRZ.</h2>

    <p class="lead">ZLINE ranges come in two families that share one platform. The Professional series covers dual-fuel (gas cooktop, electric convection oven) as RA30, RA36, and RA48, and gas-only as the SGR line. The Autograph Edition adds metallic accent trim, RAZ-30/36/48 with gold (G), champagne-bronze (CB), or matte-white (WM) handles and knobs, plus the Paramount SGRZ-36 gas range. Different trim, same core machine, same service tree.</p>

    <div class="callout-box">
      <h3>Dual-fuel oven won't heat while the burners work (the most common ZLINE range call)</h3>
      <p>On RA and RAZ dual-fuel ranges, the single most frequent call we run is burners lighting normally while the oven stays cold. That isolates the fault to the electric oven side. Our techs meter it down to one of three inexpensive parts: a failed bake element (visible break or blistering), a failed oven igniter on gas-oven variants, or an oven temperature sensor reading wrong and telling the control board to stop heating. All three are low-cost ZLINE-direct parts, and we usually complete the repair same-day. Guessing gets expensive; a meter does not.</p>
    </div>

    <p>Across the ZLINE range lineup the service tree is predictable and inexpensive:</p>

    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li><strong>Surface ignition:</strong> clicking without ignition, or one burner dead, usually a fouled or cracked igniter or a spark module. Low-cost parts, quick swap.</li>
      <li><strong>Oven not heating (dual-fuel):</strong> bake element, oven igniter, or temperature sensor, isolated by meter (above).</li>
      <li><strong>Uneven baking:</strong> convection fan motor wear or a drifting oven sensor on the electric oven cavity.</li>
      <li><strong>Broiler issues:</strong> broil element failure on the dual-fuel electric oven, straightforward replacement.</li>
      <li><strong>Control and display faults:</strong> oven control board on the electronic-oven variants, a single-board swap, far cheaper than a luxury-brand control.</li>
      <li><strong>Gas-only SGR / Paramount SGRZ:</strong> gas-oven igniter and safety valve on the oven side, surface igniters on the cooktop.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 RANGE HOODS (flagship section) -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">03, ZLINE range hood repair</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">The range hood is ZLINE's signature product, and it is a large share of our ZLINE work.</h2>

    <p class="lead">ZLINE built its name on range hoods, so we treat them as a first-class service, not a footnote. Many LA kitchens run a ZLINE hood over a different-brand range, which means hood-only calls are common. The lineup spans wall-mount, island, under-cabinet, and insert designs, in ducted and convertible (ductless) configurations.</p>

    <div class="appliance-grid">
      <div class="appliance-card">
        <h3>KB convertible wall mount (24 to 48 inch)</h3>
        <p>ZLINE's most popular hood. Stainless wall-mount, sized 24 to 48 inches, runs ducted or recirculating with a charcoal filter. On the convertible units a weak-airflow complaint is often a spent charcoal filter (a consumable people forget) before it is a motor. We confirm the mode first.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="appliance-card">
        <h3>KECOM professional wall mount (30/36/42/48)</h3>
        <p>The professional wall-mount line, KECOM-30/36/42/48, driven by a 400 or 700 CFM 4-speed motor. The blower motor is the leading failure: a motor that hums but barely spins, or won't start on lower speeds. Motor replacement is an inexpensive ZLINE-direct part.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="appliance-card">
        <h3>587 / 597 and 8654 wall series</h3>
        <p>The 587 and 597 wall hoods and the 8654 series share baffle-filter and blower architecture. Service items are the blower motor, the baffle channel and filters, and the LED lighting. Baffle filters caked with grease choke a healthy motor, so a cleaning sometimes solves a "dead" hood.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="appliance-card">
        <h3>Island and under-cabinet models</h3>
        <p>Island-mount hoods (ceiling-suspended over an island cooktop) and under-cabinet and insert units. Same core service tree, blower motor, speed control, baffle filters, LED, and damper, with access differences we work from the installed position.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="appliance-card">
        <h3>Blower motor and speed control</h3>
        <p>The 4-speed control can pit and drop a speed, mimicking a failing motor. Our techs test the control and the motor separately so you replace the part that actually failed, not both on a guess. Both are low-cost ZLINE-direct parts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="appliance-card">
        <h3>LED lighting, baffle filters, damper</h3>
        <p>LED modules and drivers fail at the light stage, not the motor. Stainless baffle filters are cleanable and cheap to replace. A stuck backdraft damper causes noise and poor draw. These are the inexpensive, fast items that keep a ZLINE hood running for years.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 MODELS -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">04, Models we service most often</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">ZLINE model families in regular SoCal rotation.</h2>

    <p class="lead">A representative sample of the ZLINE ranges and hoods our techs service routinely. Not exhaustive, the accent-color program expands the range configurations significantly, but these are the units that show up most on our route.</p>

    <div class="model-grid">
      <div class="model-card">
        <h3>Professional Dual-Fuel Ranges</h3>
        <p class="model-list">RA30 · RA36 · RA48</p>
        <p>30 / 36 / 48-inch dual-fuel (gas cooktop, electric convection oven). RA36 is the residential sweet spot. Bake element, oven sensor, and igniter are the common service items.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="model-card">
        <h3>Autograph Edition Ranges</h3>
        <p class="model-list">RAZ-30-G · RAZ-36-CB · RAZ-WM-48</p>
        <p>Same platform as the Professional RA with gold (G), champagne-bronze (CB), or matte-white (WM) accent trim. Service tree identical; trim pieces matched by exact model tag.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="model-card">
        <h3>Gas Ranges (Professional / Paramount)</h3>
        <p class="model-list">SGR30 · SGR36 · SGRZ-36</p>
        <p>Gas-only ranges including the Autograph Paramount SGRZ-36. Gas-oven igniter, safety valve, and surface igniters are the service items.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="model-card">
        <h3>KB Convertible Wall Hoods</h3>
        <p class="model-list">KB-30 · KB-36 · KB-48</p>
        <p>24 to 48-inch convertible wall mount, ducted or ductless. Blower motor, charcoal filter (ductless), baffle filters, LED.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="model-card">
        <h3>KECOM Professional Hoods</h3>
        <p class="model-list">KECOM-30 · KECOM-36 · KECOM-48</p>
        <p>Professional wall-mount, 400 or 700 CFM 4-speed motor. Blower motor and speed control are the leading service items.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="model-card">
        <h3>587 / 597 / 8654 &amp; Island Hoods</h3>
        <p class="model-list">587 · 597 · 8654 · GL series (island)</p>
        <p>Wall, island, and under-cabinet variants sharing baffle and blower architecture. Motor, baffle filters, LED, damper.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 PRICING -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">05, Pricing</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">What ZLINE repair costs in Southern California.</h2>

    <p class="lead">Diagnostic is $89, applied toward the repair when you approve the work. ZLINE sits in the value repair tier: parts are inexpensive and come direct from ZLINE with no gating, so most repairs are labor-driven and finish fast. Ranges below include labor.</p>

    <div class="pricing-grid">
      <div class="price-card">
        <div class="price-label">Diagnostic</div>
        <div class="price-amount">$89</div>
        <div class="price-desc">Waived when you approve repair</div>
      </div>
      <div class="price-card">
        <div class="price-label">Range standard band</div>
        <div class="price-amount">$160–$320</div>
        <div class="price-desc">Oven igniter · bake / broil element · surface igniter · oven sensor</div>
      </div>
      <div class="price-card">
        <div class="price-label">Range major component</div>
        <div class="price-amount">$260–$460</div>
        <div class="price-desc">Convection fan motor · gas safety valve · oven control board</div>
      </div>
      <div class="price-card">
        <div class="price-label">Range hood</div>
        <div class="price-amount">$150–$380</div>
        <div class="price-desc">Blower motor · speed control · baffle filters · LED · damper</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="price-note">Repair-versus-replace on ZLINE favors repair for almost any single-component failure. A ZLINE range runs roughly $2,000 to $4,500 new and a hood a few hundred to around a thousand, so a $200 to $450 repair on a working unit is an easy call, and the inexpensive direct parts supply is what makes it economical. The exception is major structural damage or a stacked multi-component failure on an older unit, where we lay out the full number at diagnostic and let you decide. We document the math before authorization, every time.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 06 RECENT REPAIRS -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">06, Recent repairs</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">ZLINE jobs from across the territory.</h2>

    <p class="lead">Three representative service calls, model, symptom, diagnosis, repair, and cost. Names and addresses omitted; the technical scenarios are typical of what we see on ZLINE service.</p>

    <div class="repair-grid">
      <div class="repair-card">
        <h3>ZLINE RA36 dual-fuel range, Burbank</h3>
        <p><strong>Symptom:</strong> All four cooktop burners lit and worked, but the oven would not heat on bake or convection. Unit about 4 years old.</p>
        <p><strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Burners working isolated the fault to the electric oven side. Meter check found an open bake element with a visible blister near the rear bend; oven sensor and control tested within spec.</p>
        <p><strong>Repair:</strong> Bake element replaced with an OEM ZLINE-direct part carried for the RA series. Verified bake and convection cycles reached and held setpoint.</p>
        <p><strong>Cost & time:</strong> $245 total. Same-day, completed on the diagnostic visit in about an hour.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="repair-card">
        <h3>ZLINE KECOM-36 wall hood, Irvine</h3>
        <p><strong>Symptom:</strong> Hood ran loud and barely pulled air on all four speeds. Owner had already cleaned the filters twice with no change.</p>
        <p><strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Blower motor bearing worn, motor humming but turning well below rated RPM. Speed control tested clean; baffle filters were already clean, ruling out the airflow-choke cause.</p>
        <p><strong>Repair:</strong> 4-speed blower motor replaced with the OEM ZLINE part. Verified full airflow and quiet operation across all speeds.</p>
        <p><strong>Cost & time:</strong> $310 total. Same-day, 75 minutes on-site.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="repair-card">
        <h3>ZLINE RAZ-30-G Autograph range, Pasadena</h3>
        <p><strong>Symptom:</strong> Front-left burner clicked continuously but would not light; other burners normal. Gold-accent Autograph unit, about 3 years old.</p>
        <p><strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Cracked surface igniter on the front-left burner; spark module tested clean and the other igniters were within spec. Isolated single-igniter fault.</p>
        <p><strong>Repair:</strong> Front-left igniter replaced with OEM ZLINE part. Confirmed clean spark and ignition on all burners. Gold accent trim undisturbed.</p>
        <p><strong>Cost & time:</strong> $185 total. Same-day, 50 minutes on-site.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 07 SERVICE AREAS -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">07, Where we go</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">ZLINE service across Greater Los Angeles.</h2>

    <p>ZLINE installs spread across the full territory rather than clustering in one luxury pocket, which fits the brand's value positioning. We see the Professional RA and Autograph RAZ ranges in remodeled kitchens through Pasadena, Burbank, Glendale, and the San Fernando Valley, and out into Irvine, Rancho Cucamonga, Riverside, and Santa Barbara where new-build and renovation kitchens picked ZLINE for the pro-range look at a reachable price. Range hood-only calls come from everywhere, including homes running a ZLINE KB or KECOM hood over a different-brand cooktop. Coastal addresses in the South Bay and along the Orange County coast see the usual salt-air wear on hood hardware and igniters. The 8-branch dispatch grid in the hero shows the closest territory; our techs arrive with common ZLINE igniters, elements, and hood blower motors on the truck for same-day completion when the symptom can be identified by phone first.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 08 RELATED -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">08, Related service</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">ZLINE across the repair catalog.</h2>

    <div class="related-grid">
